%T A399882 930,15,1,1,778,1,1,1,774,1,1,1,1806,110,1,1,2162,6,1,1,1354,1,1,1,
%U A399882 2070,1,1,1,3422,94,1,1,42,3,1,1,4422,1,1,1,4970,1,1,1,6
%N A399882 On Artin's conjecture, (a(n)/A399883(n))*C is the relative density of primes with primitive root -n among the primes, where C = A005596 is Artin's constant.
%C A399882 Write -n = (b^2*c)^k < -1 where b^2*c is not a prime power and c is squarefree, then a(n) is even if and only if c == 1 (mod 4). What's more, a(n) = 1 if and only if n is in A120629. See comments in A399880 for more details.
%H A399882 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399882/b399882.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A399882 Heath-Brown, <a href="https://surya-teja.com/2010/10/06/heath-brown-artin-primitive-roots-conjecture/">Artin Primitive Roots Conjecture</a>.
%H A399882 Oleksiy Klurman, Igor E. Shparlinski, and Joni Teräväinen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1112/blms.70103">On Artin's conjecture on average and short character sums</a>. Bull. London Math. Soc., 57 (2025): 2429-2443.
%H A399882 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399882/a399882.txt">Artin(n) for n = -1..-10000</a>.
%H A399882 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399880/a399880.txt">PARI code for Artin()</a>.
%H A399882 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/ArtinsConstant.html">Artin's constant</a>.
%H A399882 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artin%27s_conjecture_on_primitive_roots">Artin's conjecture on primitive roots</a>.
%H A399882 <a href="/index/Ar#Artin">Index entries for sequences related to Artin's conjecture</a>
%F A399882 See A399880.
%e A399882 Let n = -15 (c = -15, b = 1). Then:
%e A399882 - For k = 1, i.e., S = {3,5}, T empty, we have Artin(-15) = (5 * 19 - (-1) * (-1))/(5 * 19) = 94/95;
%e A399882 - For k = 3, i.e., S = {5}, T = {3}, we have Artin((-15)^3) = (19 * 3 - (-1) * (-3))/(5 * 19) = 54/95;
%e A399882 - For k = 5, i.e., S = {3}, T = {5}, we have Artin((-15)^5) = (5 * 15 - (-1) * (-5))/(5 * 19) = 14/19;
%e A399882 - For k = 15, i.e., S empty, T = {3,5}, we have Artin((-15)^15) = (3 * 15 - (-3) * (-5))/(5 * 19) = 6/19.
%o A399882 (PARI) A399882(n) = numerator(Artin(-n)) \\ See Links for Artin()
%Y A399882 Cf. A005596, A399883 (denominator), A399880/A399881 ({Artin(n)}), A120629.
